&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The role&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Lifecycle Marketing Operations Manager is an experienced Braze campaign architect responsible for asset development, audience segmentation, and campaign quality assurance in multiple marketing communication channels, including: email, SMS, push, and in-app messaging. With a strong focus on both campaign execution and stakeholder collaboration, the ideal candidate has superior attention to detail and time management skills, as well as the ability to understand business needs &amp;amp; objectives in order to consistently deliver pristine, on-time work. The LCM Ops manager will work closely with LCM strategists to recommend features, design tests, and review strategy to achieve shared OKRs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In collaboration with a Lifecycle Marketing Strategist, execute large and/or complex data-driven marketing initiatives utilizing a campaign management tool; perform activities such as campaign architecture, audience selection, trigger qualification, suppressions, segmentation and arbitration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop canvas/asset templates, segments, and playbooks for repetitive or turnkey projects. Train others and own the coding/building, approval process, and deployment of daily, monthly, and ad-hoc content-focused lifecycle marketing campaigns; contribute strategic thought leadership to the team’s campaign testing &amp;amp; optimization strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver on lifecycle campaign execution deadlines in various marketing channels (e.g. Email, Push, In-App Messaging, SMS, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document and enhance processes, best practices, and FAQs. Develop, enforce, and perform quality control activities to ensure daily campaign deployment completes in a timely manner and the output is accurate and complete&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce campaign performance reports using analytically derived model outputs to share test outcomes, highlight campaign business impact, and inform future testing strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consolidate and confirm the accuracy of prospect and/or customer audience data when building campaign audience segmentation; this includes collaborating with LCM Technical Project Managers and/or cross-functional data partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a strong relationship with strategic partners; you will act as a technical advisor to LCM strategists from planning all the way through reporting&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with others on the Lifecycle Marketing team to understand and provide tactical feedback regarding campaign objectives, data specifications, technical requirements, etc&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you’ll need:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s Degree, ideally in Business, Finance, Marketing, or a technical field (or equivalent professional experience)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of HTML coding experience, with hands-on experience building and deploying emails. Being able to code from scratch is not a requirement, but comfort with manipulating templates is.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with marketing automation tools and/or ESPs (e.g. Braze, Pardot, Marketo, Eloqua, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience proactively managing own workload and output&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest to learn new tools with a natural curiosity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diligent adherence to best practices and QA procedures, with very strong attention to detail&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate strategies, results, and insights effectively&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working independently, with little or no supervision&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nice to have:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with Data Analysts, Software Engineers, and Project Managers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience with Braze and Pardot is a strong plus&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of A/B and multivariate testing standards&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of relational databases, real-time event data, data structures and querying language (e.g. select, merge, join, group by, etc)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing SQL statements for data extraction&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with real-time web and app event data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;gmail_default&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;gmail_default&quot;&gt;The base pay range for this role is listed below. Final base pay offer will be determined based on individual factors such as the candidate’s experience, skills, and location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;gmail_default&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
